# Lateral Movement Detection Lab (WMI & Remote PowerShell)

## Scenario

Suspicious PowerShell execution was detected across multiple hosts.  
Investigation revealed that PowerShell was launched by system-level processes, suggesting possible remote execution.

This lab simulates detection of lateral movement using Windows logs in Splunk.


## Logs / Evidence

Here’s what was observed:

| _time | EventID | Host        | ParentProcessName | ProcessName     | DestinationIp |
|------|--------|------------|------------------|----------------|--------------|
| 15:10 | 4688 | Finance-PC  | wmiprvse.exe     | powershell.exe | 192.168.1.20 |
| 15:11 | 4688 | HR-PC       | wmiprvse.exe     | powershell.exe | 192.168.1.20 |
| 15:12 | 4688 | Finance-PC  | wmiprvse.exe     | powershell.exe | 192.168.1.21 |
| 15:13 | 4688 | HR-PC       | wmiprvse.exe     | powershell.exe | 192.168.1.21 |


## Detection Queries

### Detect Suspicious Parent Processes (WMI / Remote Execution)

```spl
index=lab_logs EventID=4688 ProcessName="powershell.exe"
| search ParentProcessName IN ("wmiprvse.exe","psexec.exe","services.exe")
| table _time Host ParentProcessName ProcessName Account_Name CommandLine

Detect Lateral Movement Across Hosts
index=lab_logs EventID=4688 ProcessName="powershell.exe"
| search ParentProcessName="wmiprvse.exe"
| stats count by Host DestinationIp
Detect Multiple Hosts Executing Same Behavior
index=lab_logs EventID=4688 ProcessName="powershell.exe"
| search ParentProcessName="wmiprvse.exe"
| stats dc(Host) as affected_hosts by DestinationIp
| where affected_hosts > 1
Analysis
PowerShell execution was observed on multiple hosts (Finance-PC, HR-PC).
The parent process for execution was wmiprvse.exe, a Windows service used for remote management.
Key Observations:
No direct user interaction (not launched by Word, Outlook, or Explorer)
Execution initiated by system process
Activity observed across multiple hosts
Pattern Observed:
Same execution method
Multiple systems affected
Internal IP communication
Conclusion:
This behavior is consistent with lateral movement using WMI (Windows Management Instrumentation).
An attacker likely used remote execution to move between systems after initial compromise.
What Was Done
Affected hosts (Finance-PC, HR-PC) were isolated
Suspicious administrative activity was investigated
Compromised credentials were reset
Network traffic between affected hosts was monitored and restricted
Incident escalated for full environment review

